            <div xml:id="d25">

                <pb facs="0149" n="35" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg35"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/4016: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sackett</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-20T23:00:00+01:00">June 20, 1931—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 20—10:22 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>86. Received your No. 81, June 20, 11 a.m. I at once saw the Chancellor and Under
                    Secretary von Billow after our Department conversation. The nature of the
                    desired communication is entirely understood.</p>
                <p>It has had to be prepared under pressure as Von Hindenburg is in East Prussia.
                    You will, I believe, find the draft, which I have seen, satisfactory.</p>
                <p>By midnight I expect to receive the final text and to begin encoding it.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sackett</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
